{"id":"VHH__tool__noise2d_curl","collection":"VHH","category":"tool","source_path":"VHH/tool/noise2d_curl.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::noise2d_curl"],"counts":{"nodes":57,"connections":110,"values":25,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Curl Noise - One of the pre-made noise fields. This is a standard 3d curl noise flattened in various ways for use as a scalar field.","documentation_search":"noise2d curl Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Curl Noise - One of the pre-made noise fields. This is a standard 3d curl noise flattened in various ways for use as a scalar field. Input mask Scalar field mask on the outgoing field. warp vector field Domain warp on the outgoing field. field weight Overall weight of this field from 0-1. magnitude Magnitude of the field. frequency Frequency of the field. seed The seed to use for randomization. time A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. interpolation Converts the 3d curl to a 2d scalar field. - min : Uses the minimum of the x, y and z component - max : Uses the maximum of the x, y and z component - length : Uses the length of the vector - average : Uses the average of the x, y and z adjust field An fCurve allowing you to adjust the field across values. translate Move the field. rotate Rotate the field. scale Scale the field. invert mask Inverts the scalar field mask. adjust mask A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask. warp amount The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp. sharpen When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp. At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field. step field When this is selected, the field is discretized into \"steps\". step shape The shape of the steps. Because the curve pre- and post-extrapolation is set to \"Relative Repeat\" this acts like a modulo on the field. You can vary the shape of your stepping with just the controls on this curve. step mask A scalar field input to mask area of the step field. invert step mask When this is checked, the step mask is inverted. adjust step mask An fCurve allowing adjustment of the step mask. Output curl noise field The field result ready to be used.","port_names":["adjust_field","adjust_step_mask","curl_noise_field","field_weight","frequency","interpolation","invert_mask","invert_step_mask","magnitude","mask","mask_adjust","rotate","scale","seed","sharpen","step_field","step_mask","step_shape","time","translate","warp_amount","warp_vector_field"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::build_array","Core::Array::get_from_array","Core::Conversion::degrees_to_radians","Core::Conversion::vector3_to_scalar","Core::Fields::advect_field","Core::Fields::curl_noise_field","Core::Fields::fcurve_field","Core::Fields::field_is_empty","Core::Fields::gradient_field","Core::Fields::scalar_field","Core::Fields::scale_field","Core::Fields::transform_field","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Logic::equal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::SRT_to_matrix","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::euler_to_quaternion","Core::Math::length","Core::Math::lerp","Core::Math::max","Core::Math::min","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::negate","Core::Math::one_over","Core::Math::subtract","Unknown","VHH::Core::Fields::change_range_field","adjust_the_field","maskWerks","step_funct"],"dependencies_search":["VHH::Core::Fields::change_range_field"],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::noise2d_curl","uri_imported":"stream:/bifrostGraphShape1","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/noise2d_curl.md","_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"The transforms"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The field"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The warp"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The mask"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The Adjustment"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Weights"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The steps"}]},"documentation_file":"VHH/docs/noise2d_curl.md","documentation":"### ***noise2d_curl***\n<font size = 1>**Component Compound** - this compound is a component in the the *displacer* ecosystem.<br /><br /></font>\n<font size = 2>**Curl Noise** - One of the pre-made noise fields.  This is a standard 3d curl noise flattened in various ways for use as a scalar field.</font><br />\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***mask***</span>\n<br />Scalar field mask on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***warp_vector_field***</span>\n<br />Domain warp on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***field_weight***</span>\n<br />Overall weight of this field from 0-1.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***magnitude***</span>\n<br />Magnitude of the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***frequency***</span>\n<br />Frequency of the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***seed***</span>\n<br />The seed to use for randomization.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***time***</span>\n<br />A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. \n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***interpolation***</span>\n<br />Converts the 3d curl to a 2d scalar field.\n- **min**:  Uses the minimum of the x, y and z component\n- **max**:  Uses the maximum of the x, y and z component\n- **length**:  Uses the length of the vector\n- **average**:  Uses the average of the x, y and z\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_field***</span>\n<br />An fCurve allowing you to adjust the field across values.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***translate***</span>\n<br />Move the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***rotate***</span>\n<br />Rotate the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***scale***</span>\n<br />Scale the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_mask***</span>\n<br />Inverts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_mask***</span>\n<br />A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***warp_amount***</span>\n<br />The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***sharpen***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp.  At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***step_field***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field is discretized into \"steps\".\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***step_shape***</span>\n<br />The shape of the steps.  Because the curve pre- and post-extrapolation is set to \"Relative Repeat\" this acts like a modulo on the field.  You can vary the shape of your stepping with just the controls on this curve.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***step_mask***</span>\n<br />A scalar field input to mask area of the step field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_step_mask***</span>\n<br />When this is checked, the step_mask is inverted.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_step_mask***</span>\n<br />An fCurve allowing adjustment of the step_mask.\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***curl_noise_field***</span>\n<br />The field result ready to be used.","ports":[{"name":"time","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::ScalarField"},{"name":"seed","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"0"},{"name":"translate","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"rotate","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"scale","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"1f","y":"1f","z":"1f"}},{"name":"interpolation","direction":"input","type":"int","default":"3L"},{"name":"mask","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::ScalarField"},{"name":"mask_adjust","direction":"input","type":"Math::FCurve","default":{"version":"1","preExtrapolation":"0","postExtrapolation":"0","points":[{"point":{"locked":"1","interpolation":"1","pcn":{"xp":"-0.10000000000000